            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0089" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G Commercial Agreement/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-24T22:00:00-05:00">September 24, 1934—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 25—3:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. Your circular of September 23, 2 p.m. Officials of the Colombian Ministry for
                    Foreign Affairs whom I have consulted fail to see any advantage to be derived
                    for Colombia from the Agreement which was opened for signature by the Pan
                    American Union on July 15. <pb facs="0090" n="20" xml:id="pg20"/> If the
                    Department deems it desirable to suggest any arguments, I can transmit them to
                    responsible officials.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
